    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48870.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "They are all interconnected and I'll give an example that is timely right now. You look at what's happening in Israel and the horrific terror attack on October 7th and the war that has followed it. We are seeing right now, we're seeing anti-Semitism on college campuses across the country. It is horrifying, especially our so-called elite universities. We saw MIT, Jewish students prevented from going to campus because of anti-Semitic radical activists. And then the university administration said that they would not punish, they would not expel the anti-Semitic protesters who were threatening other students. Why? Because they were there on student visas. And if they expel them, they'd lose their student visa. So these are visitors to our country and the university is terrified to stand up to them. We saw just this last week in California at USC. USC has banned a Jewish professor from coming to campus. Why? Because again, anti-Semitic radical left has threatened him. And instead of the university saying, we're going to protect our professor, they said, no, we're going to require you to teach your classes remotely because we're going to give in to the mob. And if you look at the intersection right now, number one, this is a manifestation of cultural Marxism. Marxism looks at the world as a conflict between oppressors and victims. Marx did it on a socioeconomic lens, but cultural Marxism doesn't just break it down socioeconomically. It looks at race. That's where you get critical race theory. It looks at gender and sexual orientation. That's where you get queer theory. And for the radical left, they look at Israel and they have coded Jews as oppressors. They have coded Palestinians as victims. And accordingly, the cultural Marxist supports the violent revolution of the victims against the so-called oppressors. And you were talking about the ecosystem, the intersection.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
