    "turn_text": "Well, look, truth is a powerful antidote, and it's an antidote to lies. And communism, communism is fragile. You know, I opened the book by telling my family story, telling my father's story, how as a teenager in Cuba, he fought in the communist revolution, and he fought alongside Fidel Castro. And my dad, as a teenager, was imprisoned in Cuba, he was tortured in Cuba, and he fled and came to America seeking freedom. And that day, He in particular, if you look at communist regimes, if you look at Marxist, they don't want sunlight. They're terrified of sunlight. And that's something I describe in the book, how when you simply expose what they're doing, most people recoil. And it's why they have to rely on force and coercion instead. And so, look, I want to encourage your listeners to Go online, go on to Amazon, or Barnes & Noble, or Books & Million, wherever you get your books. Go buy a copy of the book Unwoke How to Defeat Cultural Marxism in America. But let me encourage you, actually, Christmas season is coming up. The book, I think, makes a great Christmas gift. And so buy more than one. Buy a copy for your mom. Buy a copy for your best friend. Buy a copy for your crazy left-wing neighbor. to try to knock some sense into them or even better buy a copy for your kids or your grandkids. Because this book is designed, it's fun, it's readable, it has stories, it's interesting, but it's designed to be useful, to equip you to fight back against this wokeness that is doing so much damage and to give you practical steps you can do in your life to fight back.",
