    "turn_text": "And I got one of my junior papers back, and you write two of them one first semester, one second semester. I got one of them back that Robbie had graded. And the first page, the corner was folded down. and it had C plus circled. And I remember holding it and my knuckles turned white. I was literally trembling and with the super seriousness of a 19 year old, I was convinced my life was over like my entire academic career collapsed. I was gonna be a homeless person in the streets. Like it was, I just went through this sort of visions of terror. And then I flipped the corner over and robbie had written just kidding a And I went into his office. I said, Professor George, you are an evil man. And he laughed, laughed heartily. And I told that story at Princeton Reunion where Robbie was interviewing me. And he laughed again. And he said, I don't remember that at all. And I said, well, it made a much bigger impact on me than I think it did on you. And so I still say that, JP, on my bookshelf, with the corner folded down and Robbie's joke on the cover.",
